From 388ddf0b7c0743a2789af07fed6694c9644c8909 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amir Nassereldine <46420889+amirnd51@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:27:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Rename MOLA to Tutticore in the local patch series

The compiler that drives this fork renamed itself from MOLA to Tutticore
(dialect tutticore, language Tutti). Rename the names the two sides share
in lockstep: the attributes tutticore.target / tutticore.memspace /
tutticore.placement_done / tutticore.in_l1 / tutticore.lhs_l1 /
tutticore.out_l1, the pipeline options tutticore-placement-pipeline and
tutticore-pre-to-d2m-pipeline, and the TUTTICORE_TT_* switches. Comments
follow. mola-patches/ is the historical mirror and is left as it was.

Replayed onto 9b2157f (record 46, padding view zero fill) from 9d539f37,
which made the same change on b88ff0c; the five MOLA comments 816a448
added are renamed the same way.

Not built or tested here: no TT toolchain on the machine that made it.
